	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"In &6Create: Forge Frontier&r, the mod &5Apotheosis&r overhauls the vanilla system for enchanting. It does this by introducing some new stats to enchanting tables and new bookshelves to alter those stats."
				""
				"These stats are as follows:"
				"&n&aEterna&r&r"
				"&n&4Quanta&r&r"
				"&5&nArcana&r&r"
				""
				"Other modifiers that can be added are:"
				"&eRectification&r"
				"&3Enchanting Clues&r"
				"&6Treasure Enchantments&r"
			]
			id: "6965F4ABCAB88875"
			rewards: [{
				id: "48F1F245E472FD1F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 150
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 2.3d
			subtitle: "Apotheosis Enchanting"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2D29A403707CC3C6"
				item: "minecraft:book"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Introduction to Enchanting"
			x: 4.8999999999999995d
			y: -7.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6965F4ABCAB88875"]
			description: [
				"&n&5Apotheosis&r&r changes many things about Enchanting in Minecraft, yet some remain the same. "
				""
				"Enchanting tables will only detect blocks modifying it's stats if they're exactly one block away. These stats alter the behaviour of your enchantments."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&a&nEterna&r&r, also known as  Enchanting Power, determines the level of your enchantments. Different tiers and types of bookshelves will add varying amounts. Every level of shelf has a certain maximum of &a&nEterna&r&r beyond which it will no longer contribute to raising the value."
				""
				"The level of your enchantment is 2x your Eterna value. If you reach the maximum of 50 &n&aEterna&r&r you will be enchanting at level 100."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&n&4Quanta&r&r refers to the instability of your enchantments. This can be both a good and a bad thing as it can both increase or decrease the true level of enchantment that will be applied. "
				""
				"The amount it increases or decreases depends on the enchanting table's Quanta value. If the table has a Quanta value of 50, the actual enchantment value can be -50 or +50."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&n&5Arcana&r&r is the stat that determines the availability of rare enchants. The higher the value the easier it is to get rare enchants on whatever item is being enchanted. "
				""
				"However very high levels of &5&nArcana&r&r will also make common enchantments more difficult to get."
			]
			id: "2172A6251E7C57A8"
			rewards: [
				{
					exclude_from_claim_all: true
					id: "299E61F0BA970F83"
					table_id: 8678092705658131358L
					type: "choice"
				}
				{
					id: "6931E7D726999DAB"
					type: "xp_levels"
					xp_levels: 2
				}
				{
					count: 10
					id: "08F6E0B772C8A4BA"
					item: "minecraft:bookshelf"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "Enchanting Properties"
			tasks: [{
				id: "62E466E5012D5CCC"
				item: "minecraft:enchanting_table"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Apotheosis Enchanting"
			x: 5.0d
			y: -4.1000000000000005d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2172A6251E7C57A8"]
			description: [
				"&n&eRectification&r&r is a modifier that interacts with &4&nQuanta&r&r."
				""
				"The way it interacts is by stripping away the negative scalar of the random modifier. &n&4Quanta&r&r can both increase and decrease the applied level of enchantments, the higher the rectification the smaller the negative value. "
				""
				"At 100% &n&eRectification&r&r, enchantments will no longer be able to go lower, the &n&4Quanta&r&r instability can only improve their level, potentially even beyond the maximum of Level 100 at 50 &n&aEterna&r&r."
			]
			icon: "apotheosis:rectifier"
			id: "722D72A914A3A75B"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 8
					id: "436B22DE5D260776"
					item: "minecraft:amethyst_block"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
